# A game's pull-request previews (the core's README, "How a project takes the core", point 5, "A game served by GitHub
# Pages"): once the game's build has run on a pull request and uploaded the artifact "preview" (the file pr-number and,
# unless the pull request closed, the built site in site/), the core's preview.yml publishes it at pr-<number>/ on the
# gh-pages branch, links it in one comment and removes it when the pull request closes. workflow_run runs main's copy of
# this file, never a pull request's, and the core's job runs none of the pull request's code. Its job may push gh-pages,
# read the build's artifact and comment on the pull request, and nothing else.
name: preview

on:
  workflow_run:
    workflows: [{{build}}]
    types: [completed]

permissions:
  contents: read

jobs:
  preview:
    permissions:
      contents: write # the core's preview.yml pushes each preview to gh-pages
      actions: read # the artifact the build run left
      pull-requests: write # the pull request's one comment with its preview's address
    uses: {{core}}/.github/workflows/preview.yml@{{pin}}
